    <h2>Artist Statement</h2>

    <p>
        This photomontage explores the pressure of modern beauty standards and how they influence self-image.
        I combined a portrait with magazine imagery and symbolic elements such as a tape measure to represent
        unrealistic expectations placed on appearance. The reflection imagery suggests how media ideals can
        distort the way individuals see themselves.
    </p>

    <p>
        To create this piece, I used layer masks to combine multiple images without permanently deleting any
        areas, allowing me to work non-destructively. I applied the Overlay blending mode to integrate text
        into the composition and create a unified effect. Adjustment layers were used to control contrast
        and color across the entire image.
    </p>

